.TH COMMAND8-REAPER 1 "2026-07-06" "command8 0.1.0" "command8 manual"
.SH NAME
command8\-reaper \- Command|8 to Reaper OSC bridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B command8\-reaper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B command8\-reaper
bridges the Digidesign Command|8 control surface to the Reaper DAW over OSC
(via liblo). It translates normalized surface input into OSC and drives all
device feedback \(em motor faders, meters, encoder rings, LEDs and the LCD \(em
from Reaper's state, including encoder modes, Flip, navigation and the LCD grid.
.PP
The daemon self\-heals: it waits for the Command|8 to appear, exits its run loop
when the device is removed, and re\-opens on replug. Run only one bridge at a
time \(em stop any other Command|8 client first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \fB<prefix>\fR/lib/systemd/user/command8\-reaper.service
systemd
.B user
service unit. Enable with
.RB "\(oq" "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now command8\-reaper" "\(cq" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR command8\-monitor (1),
.BR command8\-mackie (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
